## FINAL DOs AND DON'Ts

*   Default to showing code blocks when an element is selected.
*   Default to CSS Selector as the output format.
*   When generating CSS selectors, avoid selectors with `#radix-`.
*   When generating CSS selectors, prefer selectors that start with `xx--` or `oo--`.
*   Use regular expressions for matching CSS selectors.
*   Walk the DOM tree to improve the generated CSS selectors.
*   When generating CSS selectors:
    *   Prefer `id`: if present, use `#id` and stop (shortest path).
    *   Prefer classes: up to 2 classes per node.
    *   Use `:nth-of-type` only when needed (multiple same-tag siblings).
    *   Ignore classes starting with `elpicker-`.
*   When generating CSS selectors, do not explicitly handle dynamic classes, data attributes, or `role`.
*   When generating CSS selectors, the following are not implemented:
    *   Uniqueness checks (e.g. `querySelector` to verify one match).
    *   Preference for `data-*` or `role` over classes.
    *   Avoidance of `:nth-of-type` when other attributes suffice.
    *   Shortest-path optimization (e.g. stopping when selector is unique).
*   Include options and config for setting up avoided and preferred CSS classes.